Source: parent proof step 2 (the kernel ρ̂(z) = c₁(1 − |z|)₊).

1. Let ρ₀(z) := max(0, 1 − ‖z‖). Then:
- ρ₀ is continuous and 0 ≤ ρ₀ ≤ 1;
- ρ₀(z) = 0 for ‖z‖ ≥ 1, and ρ₀(0) = 1;
- ρ₀ is 1-Lipschitz: |ρ₀(z) − ρ₀(z')| ≤ |(1 − ‖z‖) − (1 − ‖z'‖)| = |‖z'‖ − ‖z‖| ≤ ‖z − z'‖ (abs_max_sub_max_le_abs, abs_norm_sub_norm_le).

2. ρ₀ vanishes outside closedBall(0, 1), so it has compact support (HasCompactSupport.intro). It is continuous, nonnegative and nonzero at 0, so c₀ := ∫ρ₀ > 0 (Continuous.integral_pos_of_hasCompactSupport_nonneg_nonzero).

3. Put ρ := c₀⁻¹ρ₀ and C := c₀⁻¹ > 0. Then:
- ρ is continuous, ρ ≥ 0, and ρ(z) = 0 for ‖z‖ ≥ 1;
- ∫ρ = c₀⁻¹c₀ = 1 (integral_const_mul, inv_mul_cancel₀);
- |ρ(z)| = c₀⁻¹ρ₀(z) ≤ c₀⁻¹ = C;
- |ρ(z) − ρ(z')| = c₀⁻¹|ρ₀(z) − ρ₀(z')| ≤ C‖z − z'‖.
No special case for n = 0 is needed: Euclid 0 is a point of measure 1. ∎

